Edit the "Cursos" section to the existing Colegio San Marcos school management system.

IMPORTANT:
Maintain exactly the same visual language, design system, layout proportions, typography, spacing, colors, cards, buttons, icons, sidebar, top navigation, breadcrumbs, and overall style used in the existing screens and the previously provided GUI specification.

Do not redesign the application. The new section must look like a native part of the existing system.


COURSES PAGE:

Replace the page "Mis Cursos y Secciones Asignadas" and create a new page titled:

"Cursos"

Use the breadcrumb structure used throughout the application:

Inicio › Gestión › Cursos

Below the breadcrumb, display the page title:

"Cursos"

Add a short descriptive subtitle such as:

"Consulta y gestiona los cursos asociados a cada grado académico."

GRADE SELECTOR:

At the top of the main content area, create a clean selection control labeled:

"Grado académico"

Use a dropdown/select component consistent with the existing application's form controls.

Example options:

- 1ro Secundaria
- 2do Secundaria
- 3ro Secundaria
- 4to Secundaria
- 5to Secundaria

Initially select:

"4to Secundaria"

When the selected grade changes, the course list displayed below should update to show the courses belonging to that grade.

COURSE LIST:

Below the grade selector, display a section titled:

"Cursos de 4to Secundaria"

Present the courses as clean white cards or a structured list/table consistent with the existing application's visual style.

Each course entry must contain:

1. Course name
2. Course description
3. A button labeled exactly:

"Añadir competencias"

Example:

--------------------------------------------------
Matemáticas

Curso orientado al desarrollo del razonamiento
matemático y la resolución de problemas.

                         [ Añadir competencias ]
--------------------------------------------------

Another example:

--------------------------------------------------
Comunicación

Desarrolla competencias relacionadas con la
comprensión y producción de textos.

                         [ Añadir competencias ]
--------------------------------------------------

COURSE EXAMPLES:

For the initially selected "4to Secundaria", display courses such as:

- Matemáticas
- Comunicación
- Ciencias Sociales
- Ciencia y Tecnología
- Inglés
- Educación Física
- Arte y Cultura

Use realistic but concise descriptions for each course.

"ANADIR COMPETENCIAS" INTERACTION:

Each course must have its own "Añadir competencias" button.

When the button is clicked, open a modal or expandable panel for that specific course.

The modal/panel should clearly display:

"Competencias de [Nombre del curso]"

Include a list of available competencies with checkboxes.

For example, for Matemáticas:

☐ Resuelve problemas de cantidad
☐ Resuelve problemas de regularidad, equivalencia y cambio
☐ Resuelve problemas de forma, movimiento y localización
☐ Resuelve problemas de gestión de datos e incertidumbre

Include buttons:

[Cancelar] [Guardar competencias]

The interaction should visually follow the existing form, checkbox, modal, and button patterns from the GUI specification.

VISUAL DESIGN:

Use the existing design system:

- Primary Deep Blue: #00236f
- Secondary Blue: #0058be
- Application background: #f8f9ff
- Cards and surfaces: #ffffff
- Main text: #121c2a
- Success Green: #16a34a
- Warning Amber: #d97706
- Danger Red: #ba1a1a

Use the existing typography hierarchy:

- Headline LG: 24px / 32px / Bold
- Headline MD: 18px / 24px / Semi Bold
- Headline SM: 16px / 24px / Regular
- Body MD: 14px / 20px / Regular
- Label SM: 12px / 16px / Medium
- Label XS: 11px / 16px / Medium / Uppercase

Use the same 4px spacing scale already established in the design system.

LAYOUT:

Keep the existing top navigation bar unchanged.

Keep the content area spacious and aligned with the application's existing 24px layout margins and grid.

The page should visually resemble the existing "Horarios", "Auditorías", and other administrative pages.

The overall hierarchy should be:

Breadcrumb
    ↓
Page title + description
    ↓
Grade selector
    ↓
Course count / contextual information
    ↓
Course list
    ↓
Course cards
        ├── Course name
        ├── Description
        └── [Añadir competencias]

RESPONSIVE BEHAVIOR:

On desktop, display the course cards in a clean vertical list or a two-column card layout if it fits naturally with the existing design.

On smaller screens, stack the cards vertically.

The grade selector should remain easy to use on mobile.

Do not introduce horizontal scrolling.

IMPORTANT CONSTRAINTS:

- Keep the existing sidebar and top navigation design.
- Do not remove or rename existing navigation items.
- Add "Cursos" under "GESTIÓN".
- Do not modify the existing "Horarios" page.
- Do not modify the existing "Auditorías" or "Log de errores" functionality.
- Do not introduce unnecessary filters.
- Do not add fields such as IP, Nivel, or Estado to this new section.
- Keep the interface clean, professional, and consistent with the existing Colegio San Marcos system.
- The final screen should look as if "Cursos" had always been part of the original application.